cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QKPCG-L, please cite it as below, together with the sources of its data listed in README.md."
title: "QKPCG-L: large instances of the quadratic knapsack problem with conflict graphs"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "García"
    given-names: "José"
version: "1.0.1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23325516"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/rubincus/QKPCG-L"
abstract: >-
  Fifty instances of the quadratic knapsack problem with conflict graphs with 1500 and 2000 items,
  derived from Set I of the disjunctively constrained knapsack problem by adding quadratic profits
  drawn uniformly from {1, ..., 50}. The release includes the generation seeds and SHA-256 digests,
  reference values obtained from published DCKP solution certificates, and tools to verify solutions,
  regenerate the instances and recompute the reference values.
keywords:
  - quadratic knapsack problem
  - conflict graph
  - disjunctively constrained knapsack problem
  - benchmark instances
  - combinatorial optimization
